  "name": "Track client reply SLAs in Gmail with OpenAI triage, Google Sheets and Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ca42bf1d-3c56-41b9-9698-ff5d1cbc15f2",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1180,
        "content": "## Track client reply SLAs in Gmail with OpenAI triage, Google Sheets and Slack\n\n**Who's it for**\nAgencies, consultants and freelancers who lose trust (and retainers) when a client email sits unanswered. There's no CRM needed: it works straight from Gmail, and it builds a response-time record per client over time.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Every hour it reads recent inbox and sent mail from Gmail.\n2. **Find threads waiting on you** matches them by thread. Each client thread is marked as either **waiting** (the newest message is from the client and you haven't replied) or **replied**. Colleagues, newsletters and no-reply senders are ignored.\n3. Threads are compared with the **Reply Log** sheet, so nothing is alerted twice:\n   - **New**: a thread past your reply target goes to OpenAI. It skips FYIs and thank-yous, rates priority and writes a one-line summary. Real obligations are logged and posted to Slack.\n   - **Escalated**: a thread still unanswered at 2x the target is marked overdue and re-posted.\n   - **Replied**: once you answer, the row is closed with your actual response time in hours.\n4. The Reply Log becomes your response-time record per client, ready for account reviews.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Create a Google Sheet tab named `Reply Log` with these headers: inbound_message_id, thread_id, client_email, client_domain, subject, summary, priority, stage, status, received_at, flagged_at, replied_at, response_hours.\n2. Fill in **Configure settings**: your email, internal domains, reply target in hours, Sheet ID and Slack channel. Optionally list `client_domains` to watch only those clients.\n3. Connect Gmail (both Gmail nodes), Google Sheets, OpenAI and Slack credentials, then activate.\n\n**Requirements**\nGmail, Google Sheets, an OpenAI API key and Slack.\n\n**How to customize**\n- Change the Gmail search to watch one label or a shared inbox.\n- Set different reply targets per client in **Find threads waiting on you**.\n- Add a weekly Slack summary of average response hours per client from the Reply Log."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
